Query: What historical events occurred in Kaliningrad Oblast after 1945?
Ground Truth: After 1945, the Kaliningrad Oblast was annexed by the Soviet Union and made part of the Russian SFSR. The German population was expelled and replaced by ethnic Russians, Belarusians, and Ukrainians. The Soviets pursued a policy of eliminating German history, replacing all German place names with Russian ones. The area became a closed military zone, inaccessible to foreigners and requiring special permission for Soviet citizens. In 1967, the remnants of Königsberg Castle were demolished to make way for the 'House of the Soviets'.
